{number: 59}
{title: Rescue the Perishing}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C] Rescue the perishing, [F] care for the dying,
[C] Snatch them in pity from [G7] sin and the grave;
[C] Weep o’er the erring one, [F] lift up the fallen,
[C] Tell them of Jesus the [G7] mighty to [C] save.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
Rescue the [G7] perishing,
Care for the [C] dying;
[F] Jesus is [C] merciful,
[G7] Jesus will [C] save.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[C] Tho’ they are slighting Him, [F] still He is waiting,
[C] Waiting the penitent [G7] child to receive;
[C] Plead with them earnestly, [F] plead with them gently,
[C] He will forgive if they [G7] only be-[C] lieve.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[C] Down in the human heart, [F] crushed by the tempter,
[C] Feelings lie buried that [G7] grace can restore;
[C] Touched by a loving heart, [F] wakened by kindness,
[C] Chords that were broken will [G7] vibrate once [C] more.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
[C] Rescue the perishing, [F] duty demands it;
[C] Strength for thy labor the [G7] Lord will provide;
[C] Back to the narrow way [F] patiently win them;
[C] Tell the poor wanderer a [G7] Saviour has [C] died.
{end_of_verse}
